.TH "tangsible-hosts" "1" "2026-09-05" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
tangsible-hosts - browse every inventory host
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBtangsible hosts\fR [\fIplaybook.\&yml\fR] [\fIansible-playbook args\fR .\&.\&.\&]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBhosts\fR lists every host reported by \fBansible-inventory --list\fR, and opens
the same five-tab detail view \fBtangsible-host\fR(1) shows for whichever one
you select.\& If \fIplaybook.\&yml\fR is omitted, it is resolved the same way as
\fBtangsible-run\fR(1) (see \fBtangsible\fR(1)).\&
.PP
Standard \fBansible-playbook\fR(1) arguments can be used, e.\&g.\& \fB--inventory\fR or
\fB--tags\fR can be provided.\&
.PP
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.PP
\fBUp/Down, Page Up/Down, CTRL-B/F, Home/End, CTRL-A/E\fR
.RS 4
Move the selection in the list.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBEnter\fR
.RS 4
Open the selected host'\&s detail view.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBEsc\fR
.RS 4
From the detail view, clears an active search if there is one;
otherwise goes back to the list.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBTab / Shift-Tab\fR
.RS 4
Switch tabs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB/\fR
.RS 4
Search the active tab'\&s text.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBn / N\fR
.RS 4
Jump to the next / previous match when search is active.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBq / Ctrl-C\fR
.RS 4
Quit.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Normal exit, however the view was closed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
The inventory couldn'\&t be listed, it reported no hosts at all, or
unable to write the stub playbook to create the Plays tab.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBtangsible\fR(1), \fBtangsible-host\fR(1)
